# Personal: Vertrag, Zeugnisse, Bewerbungen, Gespräche, Onboarding, UK-Variante (siehe README.md)
# Cover*: Eintrag 1 bis 4 = Quereinsteigerin, Berufsanfänger, erfahrener Grafiker, Werkstudentin.
@{
    ContractParagraph = @(
        @{ Title = '1. Start and probation'; Text = 'This statement sets out the main terms of employment between {Firma} (the Company) and {Mitarbeiter} (you). Employment begins on {Eintritt} and is permanent.
The first six months are probation; during it either side may give one week''s notice.' }
        @{ Title = '2. Job title and place of work'; Text = 'You are employed as {Stelle}. Duties are set out in the job description; other reasonable duties may be assigned.
Your place of work is the {Standort} office. Working from home: up to two days a week.' }
        @{ Title = '3. Hours of work'; Text = 'Normal hours are 37.5 a week, Monday to Friday, flexitime with core hours 10:00 to 15:00.
Extra hours before print and exhibition deadlines are taken as time off in lieu within three months, otherwise paid. The Working Time Regulations 1998 apply.' }
        @{ Title = '4. Pay'; Text = 'Your gross monthly salary is {Betrag}, paid on the last working day of the month after tax and National Insurance, plus £25.00 a month towards public transport.
Bonuses, such as a Christmas bonus, are discretionary and create no entitlement for future years.' }
        @{ Title = '5. Holiday'; Text = 'Holiday is 25 working days a year plus bank holidays, which includes the statutory 5.6 weeks. 24 and 31 December are extra days off.
Holiday is agreed with the head of office. Before the Christmas mailings go out, holiday is granted only in exceptional cases.' }
        @{ Title = '6. Sickness absence'; Text = 'Report any absence at once; if ill, phone the head of office by 9:30 on the first day. A message in the group chat is not enough.
For up to seven calendar days you self-certify; from the eighth day you need a fit note from your doctor. Statutory Sick Pay (SSP) applies; there is no contractual sick pay on top.' }
        @{ Title = '7. Other work'; Text = 'Paid outside work must be notified in writing beforehand and may be refused if it affects your work or competes with the agency. You must not work for clients of {Firma} on your own account.' }
        @{ Title = '8. Confidentiality and data protection'; Text = 'Unpublished campaigns, quotes, costings and client data stay confidential, also after your employment ends.
Work files are stored only on the file server, never on personal devices, USB sticks or private cloud storage. The IT policy forms part of these terms. Your personal data is processed under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.' }
        @{ Title = '9. Intellectual property'; Text = 'All work you create in your employment, such as drafts, layouts, photos and copy, belongs to the Company, including the right to edit it and pass it to clients; your salary covers this. You waive your moral rights as far as the law allows.
Work may appear in your own portfolio only once the client has published it and management has agreed.' }
        @{ Title = '10. Notice and disciplinary rules'; Text = 'After probation you give one month''s notice. The Company gives one month, or the statutory notice under the Employment Rights Act 1996 if longer.
Notice must be given by signed letter; an email is not enough. Disciplinary and grievance procedures follow the ACAS Code and are in the staff handbook.
Laptop, keys and access card are returned on your last day.' }
        @{ Title = '11. Pension'; Text = 'You will be enrolled automatically in the workplace pension under the Pensions Act 2008: 3 % from the Company, 5 % from you, on qualifying earnings. You may opt out within one month.' }
        @{ Title = '12. General'; Text = 'Changes are confirmed in writing within one month. No collective agreement applies. The law of England and Wales applies.
{Mitarbeiter} has received a copy of this statement, the job description and the IT policy.' }
    )
